# Monitor: BeeGFS client (`beegfs_client`)

## Detection

- Enumerate mounts with fstype **`beegfs`** or **`beegfs_nodev`** (`/proc/mounts`).
- Device id is the **mount path** (e.g. `/scratch`).
- `/proc/fs/beegfs/<clientID>/` on BeeGFS **7.3.x** exposes config/state only: **no** I/O or op counters (the client's RPC counters exist only in `BEEGFS_DEBUG` builds). Do not invent procfs counter parsers.

## Capacity (cheap, every sample)

- `statvfs(3)` on the mount -> `fs_bytes_*` / `fs_files_*` (same semantics as `lustre_llite`).

## I/O bytes (`beegfs_tcp.c`)

- **Never query the servers.** `beegfs-ctl --clientstats` makes every storage/meta server dump its whole per-client table on each call (`--filter` is client-side), so N nodes polling cost N full-table dumps per interval. Do not reintroduce it, or any other per-node server request.
- `vfs_write_bytes` / `vfs_read_bytes` = `tcpi_bytes_acked` / `tcpi_bytes_received` of the client's **established IPv4 TCP sockets** to its storage servers, read through one `NETLINK_SOCK_DIAG` dump per refresh (unprivileged; no fork, no DNS). Measured on LS6 7.3.4: within 0.03% of 1 GiB direct I/O.
- Peers come from `<instance>/storage_nodes` (`Connections: TCP: n (ip:port);` per node). Map the mount to its instance by matching `<instance>/config` `cfgFile` with the mount's `cfgFile=` option; else the only instance; else `NOT_PRESENT`.
- **Untracked listings publish `NOT_PRESENT`, never 0 or a partial total:** RDMA or SDP connections (that traffic bypasses TCP), a `TCP:` count without an endpoint, a node with no readable `Connections:` line, a truncated listing, more endpoints than the peer table, or fewer matched sockets than the listed TCP connection counts (the client prints only the first address per server, so a multi-homed server's other addresses are invisible). All nodes `<none>` (idle) is a real 0 growth.
- Totals are monotonic: per-socket growth keyed by socket cookie, a new or reset socket adds its full counters (`beegfs_tcp_acc_update`). A dump error maps through `stats_sentinel_for_errno` (`EOPNOTSUPP` for a kernel without `NETLINK_SOCK_DIAG` or byte counters -> `NOT_PRESENT`, which is also what qemu-user gives, so the live-dump tests assert that path there; `ENOBUFS` more sockets than the table -> `READ_FAILED`).
- The 15 `vfs_*_ops` keys stay in the schema and publish `NOT_PRESENT` (no client-side source).
- **Jitter:** when `enable_slow_tier` is on, refresh only on **`COLLECT_FULL`**; when off, at most once per `max(sample_freq, 30s)`. Skipped ticks re-publish the cached totals or code. No allocation in the collect path beyond the one per-mount accumulator.

## Configure

- **`--enable-beegfs`** default **yes**; `MONITOR_WITH_BEEGFS`; capability slug fragment **`beegfs`**.

## Tests

- `test_beegfs_tcp.c`: listing parser (untracked cases), accumulator, live loopback dump.
- `test_beegfs_io.c`: publish/republish, cfgFile mapping, RDMA and unmatched mounts `NOT_PRESENT`, idle listing 0.
- `test_beegfs_mount.c`: fstype and `cfgFile=` helpers. `test_fault_inject_fs.c`: failure sites.

